            <ArticleTitle>Coronary arterial rupture during coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>902-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) appears to be a relative safe and effective procedure, reported complications include coronary occlusion and dissection with or without acute myocardial infarction. Herein, a hitherto unreported complication of PTCA is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
